---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Window from "../../components/Window.astro";
import aiCreate from "../../assets/img/onebotads-ai-create.webp";
import campaigns from "../../assets/img/onebotads-campaigns.webp";
import stats from "../../assets/img/onebotads-stats.webp";
import architecture from "../../assets/img/onebotads-architecture.webp";
---

<Base
  title="OneBotAds — case study — Ayach Youssef"
  description="How I built OneBotAds: an AI-powered ad-automation SaaS with six platform integrations, built from an empty backend to production in a three-month sprint."
>
  <!-- ============ TITLE ============ -->
  <section class="study-head container">
    <p class="eyebrow">
      Case study — final-year internship (PFE), Jobistart, 2026
    </p>
    <h1 class="display">OneBotAds</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An AI-powered ad-automation SaaS: media buyers connect their Meta, TikTok,
      Google, Snapchat, LinkedIn and Taboola accounts and run every campaign
      from one dashboard — or describe the campaign in chat and let the agent
      build it.
    </p>

    <div class="meta-band">
      <div class="meta-cell">
        <span class="eyebrow">Role</span>
        <p>Sole engineer on the backend — everything below the mockup</p>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-cell">
        <span class="eyebrow">Timeline</span>
        <p>April 2026 — ongoing; live since June 23, 2026</p>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-cell">
        <span class="eyebrow">Stack</span>
        <p>
          React &middot; Node.js/Express &middot; PostgreSQL &middot; Sequelize
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-cell">
        <span class="eyebrow">Status</span>
        <p>
          Live at <a href="https://onebotads.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >onebotads.net</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ THE STARTING POINT ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The starting point</p>
        <h2 class="display">A mockup with nothing behind it</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>
          When I joined, OneBotAds was a React interface you could click through
          — and that was all. No database, no API, no connected ad platform, no
          business logic. Every screen was a promise with nothing behind it.
        </p>
        <p>
          My internship brief was to make the promise real. In under three
          months I designed and built the entire technical foundation: <strong
            >OAuth integrations for six ad platforms</strong
          >, a <strong>17-table PostgreSQL schema</strong> designed from scratch,
          <strong>~35 API route groups</strong> and <strong>~29 services</strong
          >, payments, and the AI layer that became the product&rsquo;s flagship
          feature.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ WHAT I BUILT ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What I built</p>
        <h2 class="display">Six systems, one product</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="capabilities">
        <article class="card reveal" style="--index: 0">
          <h3>Platform integrations</h3>
          <p>
            Full OAuth 2.0 flows plus campaign CRUD against the real APIs of
            Meta, TikTok, Google Ads, Snapchat, LinkedIn and Taboola — each with
            its own token lifecycle, handled by a refresh service that knows the
            rules per platform.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag tag-blue">OAuth 2.0</span><span
              class="tag tag-blue">6 platform APIs</span
            >
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card reveal" style="--index: 1">
          <h3>AI campaign agent</h3>
          <p>
            The flagship: a chat assistant that turns a conversation into a
            launch-ready campaign — filling budgets, audiences, schedules and
            creatives into the real form. Powered by an LLM orchestrating six
            MCP tool servers.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag tag-red">LLM agent</span><span class="tag tag-red"
              >6 MCP servers</span
            >
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card reveal" style="--index: 2">
          <h3>Rule engine</h3>
          <p>
            Automatic guardrails for running campaigns — pause, boost or alert
            on metric thresholds, executed by scheduled jobs every few minutes
            across all connected platforms.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag tag-yellow">node-cron</span><span
              class="tag tag-yellow">automation</span
            >
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card reveal" style="--index: 3">
          <h3>Revenue attribution</h3>
          <p>
            The pipeline that answers &ldquo;did this ad actually make
            money?&rdquo; — Shopify orders matched through UTM parameters back
            to the exact campaign, producing real ROAS instead of
            platform-reported estimates.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag tag-green">Shopify</span><span
              class="tag tag-green">UTM &rarr; ROAS</span
            >
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card reveal" style="--index: 4">
          <h3>Creative generation</h3>
          <p>
            Ad images and video generated in-app from a text prompt, integrated
            directly into the ad form — Google Imagen and Veo, plus Kling and
            Higgsfield for video.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag">Imagen 3</span><span class="tag">Veo 3</span>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card reveal" style="--index: 5">
          <h3>Payments &amp; wallet</h3>
          <p>
            Stripe and Revolut checkout with webhook-driven wallet credit, plan
            limits and a cost manager that tracks spend across every connected
            account.
          </p>
          <div class="tags">
            <span class="tag">Stripe</span><span class="tag">webhooks</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ SCREENSHOTS ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The product</p>
        <h2 class="display">In the interface</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="shots">
        <div class="reveal">
          <Window
            title="Create Ad — Use AI"
            src={aiCreate}
            alt="The AI assistant chat filling a complete campaign form: name, objective, per-platform budgets for Meta and LinkedIn, audience targeting with a live 1.4 to 1.7 million people estimate, and the ad creative"
            caption="Describe the campaign in chat; the agent fills the entire form — budgets per platform, targeting, schedule, creative — then launches it against the real APIs."
          />
        </div>
        <div class="shots-pair">
          <div class="reveal" style="--index: 0">
            <Window
              title="Campaign Manager"
              src={campaigns}
              alt="Campaign Manager table listing active campaigns across Meta, Taboola and TikTok with spend, impressions, clicks and budget columns"
              caption="Every platform's campaigns in one table — filter, search, pause and resume without leaving the app."
            />
          </div>
          <div class="reveal" style="--index: 1">
            <Window
              title="Statistics"
              src={stats}
              alt="Statistics overview with spend, impressions, clicks, CTR and CPC tiles and a per-platform performance breakdown"
              caption="Cross-platform performance rolled up into one view: spend, impressions, CTR, CPC, per platform."
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ ARCHITECTURE ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 class="display">Architecture</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>
          A React 18 client talks to a single Express server over a REST API
          with JWT auth. The server is organised in layers: route handlers
          validate and delegate to services (auth, sync, token refresh, rule
          engine, payments, stats), and only services touch the database —
          PostgreSQL through Sequelize. Scheduled jobs sync platform data every
          five minutes and run the rule engine every fifteen.
        </p>
        <p>
          The AI layer runs as <strong>MCP servers spawned per request</strong> —
          separate processes for Meta, TikTok and Google tools, so the agent&rsquo;s
          capabilities are isolated from the main API and can fail without taking
          it down. External clouds hang off the edges: the six ad-platform APIs, the
          AI and creative providers, and Stripe webhooks for payments.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal" style="margin-top: var(--space-12)">
        <Window
          title="OneBotAds — system architecture"
          src={architecture}
          alt="System architecture diagram: React 18 client, Express server with 35 route handlers and 29 services, PostgreSQL with 17 tables via Sequelize, MCP CLI servers spawned per request, and external clouds for ad platforms, AI and creative providers, payments and automation"
          caption="The full system: client, API, database, per-request MCP servers, and the external services at the edges."
        />
      </div>
      <p class="arch-note reveal">
        Deployed on a Linux VPS with PM2 and nginx. Two editions ship from one
        codebase: the full trueROAS edition and the reduced edition currently in
        production.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ OUTCOME ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Outcome</p>
        <h2 class="display">Shipped, documented, handed over</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>
          OneBotAds went live at
          <a href="https://onebotads.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >onebotads.net</a
          >
          on June 23, 2026. A week later I delivered a complete handoff: the source,
          a documented 17-table schema, environment references, deployment procedure,
          API reference with Postman collections, and per-topic guides — so the next
          engineer can run, deploy and extend the product without me in the room.
        </p>
        <p>
          The product and source code belong to Jobistart; this page shows my
          role, the architecture, and the shipped result.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="featured-actions reveal" style="margin-top: var(--space-12)">
        <a
          href="https://onebotads.net"
          class="btn btn-primary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Visit the live product</a
        >
        <a href="/#contact" class="btn">Work with me</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
